    "Use YAML for configuration files (U2, U8) because Spring Boot provides first-class YAML support.",
    "Implement jdbchdfs passthrough mode (U3) by introducing a new Step implementation that bypasses chunk-oriented processing and directly streams data.",
    "Decouple execution context from job launch lifecycle in Spring Batch (U4) by introducing an ExecutionContextManager interface and modifying JobLauncher to use it, allowing custom serialization strategies.",
    "Support Java Config job modules (U5) by enhancing the module deployer to scan for @Configuration classes containing @Bean methods of type Job, and register them as job definitions.",
    "Design pluggable SPI for cloud deployments (U6) using Spring's SpringFactoriesLoader mechanism, defining a CloudDeployerSPI interface with ReceptorAPIDeployer as one implementation.",
    "Add shortDescription field to module metadata (U7) by extending the module.yml schema and updating the documentation generator to include it in the module index.",
    "For HDFS-hosted Python scripts (U8), use Hadoop FileSystem API to read script content, write to a temporary local file, execute via ProcessBuilder, and capture stdout/stderr as feedback."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has full access to Spring XD and Spring Batch source code and can contribute changes upstream.",
    "The existing wiki is hosted on Confluence and can be exported via its REST API or manual export.",
    "Hadoop namenode configuration consists of host, port, and optional Kerberos settings.",
    "The jdbchdfs batch job is an existing Spring XD module that currently uses chunk-oriented processing.",
    "Spring Batch fix (U4) will be developed in a feature branch, released, and then Spring XD will upgrade its dependency.",
    "Custom job module (U5) uses Spring's @EnableBatchProcessing and standard Java Config patterns.",
    "Lattice/Diego PoC (U6) is at an early stage; the SPI design starts from scratch but must accommodate the existing Receptor API integration.",
    "Module documentation (U7) resides in a consistent location (e.g., each module's src/main/docs) and follows a common template.",
    "Shell processor module (U8) already exists and can execute local commands; HDFS integration is additive.",
    "Development environment (JDK 17+, Maven/Gradle, IDE) is already set up.",
    "Unit and integration test infrastructure (JUnit, TestContainers, embedded Hadoop) is available.",
    "No major architectural refactoring beyond the described stories is required."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze existing wiki structure and content",
      "activity_description": "Review the current wiki (Confluence) to understand the content hierarchy, identify pages to migrate, and plan the target repository structure.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.2",
      "activity_name": "Export wiki content to Markdown/AsciiDoc",
      "activity_description": "Use Confluence export tools or scripts to convert wiki pages to Markdown or AsciiDoc format, preserving formatting and cross-references.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.3",
      "activity_name": "Organize content in project repository",
      "activity_description": "Create a directory structure under the project repo (e.g., docs/) and place exported files, adjusting links and images as needed.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.4",
      "activity_name": "Update build scripts to include documentation",
      "activity_description": "Modify Maven/Gradle build to process documentation (e.g., using Asciidoctor or MkDocs) and package it with the distribution.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.5",
      "activity_name": "Verify documentation builds correctly",
      "activity_description": "Run the documentation build locally and in CI to ensure all pages render without errors and navigation works.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.1",
      "activity_name": "Design Hadoop namenode configuration schema",
      "activity_description": "Define a YAML schema for namenode connection details (host, port, HA settings, authentication) and decide on file location (e.g., config/hadoop.yml).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.2",
      "activity_name": "Implement config file reading in DSL session initialization",
      "activity_description": "Modify the DSL session startup code to load the YAML config, create a Hadoop Configuration object, and make it available to the session context.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.3",
      "activity_name": "Add default config file template",
      "activity_description": "Provide a sample hadoop.yml.template with commented examples for common setups (standalone, HA, Kerberos).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.4",
      "activity_name": "Test with various Hadoop namenode configurations",
      "activity_description": "Validate the automatic configuration against single namenode, HA namenodes, and secured clusters (if feasible).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3.1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze current chunk processing in jdbchdfs job",
      "activity_description": "Examine the existing Spring Batch step configuration for the jdbchdfs job to understand chunk size, readers, writers, and overhead.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3.2",
      "activity_name": "Design passthrough mode",
      "activity_description": "Design a new Step implementation or configuration option that disables chunk processing and streams rows directly from JDBC to HDFS.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3.3",
      "activity_name": "Implement passthrough mode in Spring Batch / XD batch module",
      "activity_description": "Code the passthrough step, integrate with the jdbchdfs module, and expose a configuration flag (e.g., passthrough=true).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3.4",
      "activity_name": "Unit test passthrough mode",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests verifying that chunk processing is bypassed, data flows correctly, and performance improves.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3.5",
      "activity_name": "Integration test with HDFS",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end tests against a real HDFS cluster (or MiniDFSCluster) to ensure data integrity and proper resource cleanup.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze execution context and job launch coupling in Spring Batch",
      "activity_description": "Study the Spring Batch source code (JobLauncher, JobExecution, ExecutionContext) to identify serialization and classloader issues.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.2",
      "activity_name": "Design decoupling solution",
      "activity_description": "Propose an ExecutionContextManager SPI, define serialization strategy interfaces, and plan changes to JobLauncher and JobRepository.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.3",
      "activity_name": "Implement changes in Spring Batch core",
      "activity_description": "Modify Spring Batch classes to use the new SPI, ensure backward compatibility, and add configuration hooks.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.4",
      "activity_name": "Write tests for new behavior in Spring Batch",
      "activity_description": "Add unit and integration tests covering custom ExecutionContextManager implementations, serialization, and classloader isolation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.5",
      "activity_name": "Upgrade Spring XD to new Spring Batch version",
      "activity_description": "Update Spring XD's dependency to the patched Spring Batch release, resolve any version conflicts.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.6",
      "activity_name": "Refactor XD workaround (XD-2486) to use new Batch functionality",
      "activity_description": "Remove the existing workaround code in Spring XD and replace it with the standard Spring Batch SPI configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.7",
      "activity_name": "Integration test XD with upgraded Batch",
      "activity_description": "Run Spring XD test suite and specific job launch scenarios to verify CL and serialization errors are resolved.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5.1",
      "activity_name": "Investigate deployment error (job not found)",
      "activity_description": "Reproduce the error, analyze module deployment logs, and identify why Java Config job modules are not recognized.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5.2",
      "activity_name": "Modify module deployment to support Java Config job modules",
      "activity_description": "Enhance the module deployer to scan JARs for @Configuration classes with @Bean Job definitions and register them.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5.3",
      "activity_name": "Update module metadata detection for Java Config",
      "activity_description": "Extend the module metadata (module.yml or manifest) to allow explicit declaration of Java Config job classes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5.4",
      "activity_name": "Test custom job module deployment and launch",
      "activity_description": "Deploy the sample CustomBatchModule, launch the job, and verify it runs without the 'job doesn't exist' error.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5.5",
      "activity_name": "Document Java Config module creation",
      "activity_description": "Add a section to the developer guide showing how to create a custom job module using Java Config.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.1",
      "activity_name": "Review current Lattice/Diego integration",
      "activity_description": "Examine the existing PoC code to understand how the Receptor API is used and identify coupling points.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.2",
      "activity_name": "Design pluggable SPI for cloud deployments",
      "activity_description": "Define a CloudDeployerSPI interface with methods for app deployment, scaling, logging, etc., and decide on discovery mechanism (SpringFactoriesLoader).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.3",
      "activity_name": "Implement SPI framework in Spring XD",
      "activity_description": "Create the SPI interfaces, base classes, and auto-configuration to load implementations from the classpath.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.4",
      "activity_name": "Implement Receptor API as one SPI implementation",
      "activity_description": "Refactor the existing Lattice/Diego code into a ReceptorApiDeployer class implementing CloudDeployerSPI.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.5",
      "activity_name": "Test with Lattice/Diego and other potential implementations",
      "activity_description": "Validate the SPI works with the Receptor API implementation and write a mock implementation to test pluggability.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.6",
      "activity_name": "Document SPI for contributors",
      "activity_description": "Write documentation explaining how to implement a custom CloudDeployerSPI and register it.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7.1",
      "activity_name": "Identify all modules and their documentation files",
      "activity_description": "List all Spring XD modules (source, sink, processor, job, etc.) and locate their documentation (README, module.yml, etc.).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7.2",
      "activity_name": "Add shortDescription field to each module's documentation",
      "activity_description": "Edit each module's documentation file to include a concise shortDescription (1-2 sentences) describing the module's purpose.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7.3",
      "activity_name": "Update documentation generation to include shortDescription",
      "activity_description": "Modify the doc build process (e.g., Asciidoctor templates) to extract and display shortDescription in the module index.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7.4",
      "activity_name": "Review and verify all modules have shortDescription",
      "activity_description": "Run the doc build, check the generated module index, and ensure no module is missing a shortDescription.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8.1",
      "activity_name": "Design HDFS file reading mechanism for shell processor",
      "activity_description": "Define how the shell processor will reference HDFS paths (e.g., hdfs://namenode/path/script.py), handle authentication, and cache scripts locally.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8.2",
      "activity_name": "Implement HDFS client integration in shell processor module",
      "activity_description": "Add Hadoop FileSystem dependency, implement a service to fetch script content from HDFS to a temporary file before execution.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8.3",
      "activity_name": "Add configuration for HDFS paths and Python runtime",
      "activity_description": "Extend shell processor configuration (YAML) to specify HDFS script location, Python interpreter path, and any arguments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8.4",
      "activity_name": "Implement script execution and feedback capture",
      "activity_description": "Execute the Python script via ProcessBuilder, capture stdout/stderr, and return them as the processor's output message payload.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8.5",
      "activity_name": "Test with sample Python scripts on HDFS",
      "activity_description": "Deploy test scripts to HDFS, run the shell processor in a stream, verify output and error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8.6",
      "activity_name": "Document usage",
      "activity_description": "Add documentation for the new HDFS script feature, including configuration examples and limitations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Set up development environment and build",
      "activity_description": "Ensure the developer's environment is configured for all modules (Spring XD, Spring Batch, Hadoop client), including IDE and build tools.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "General testing and bug fixing across all stories",
      "activity_description": "Address bugs found during development, run existing test suites to prevent regressions, and fix any integration issues.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing of all features together",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end tests combining multiple new features (e.g., custom job module with HDFS script, passthrough job with new Batch).",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Prepare release notes and final documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write release notes summarizing the increment, update user guides, and ensure all documentation is versioned with the code.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 282
  }
}

